// A SAPIC conditional whose formula is wider than one line.
//
// A conditional renders its formula STANDALONE: `prettySapicComb (Cond a) =
// "if " ++ render (prettySyntacticSapicFormula a)`
// (Theory/Sapic/Process.hs:476#prettySapicComb, reaching
// Theory/Sapic/Term.hs:174-175#prettySyntacticSapicFormula), and `render` is
// HughesPJ's default page — 100 columns, ribbon 67.  The conjunction node's
// `sep [opParens p' <-> ppOp op, opParens q']`
// (Theory/Model/Formula.hs:493-496, inside
// Theory/Model/Formula.hs:474-514#prettyLFormula) therefore breaks, and the
// second conjunct starts a new line at column 0.  Each conjunct here is 62
// characters wide, so the conjunction needs 127 and does not fit; the port
// builds the same text with a flat string builder and takes no break.
//
// One rendering feeds two outputs (Sapic/Facts.hs:376-388#toRule): the
// `process=` rule attribute reprints the step verbatim, while the derived
// rule name is `filter isAlpha` over the same string
// (Sapic/Facts.hs:401#stripNonAlphanumerical) and drops the line break — so
// both engines name the two rules
// `ifLongeraaaaaaaaaaxxxxxxxxxxbbbbbbbbbbyyyyyyyyyyLongercccccccccczzzzzzzzzzaaaaaaaaaayyyyyyyyyy_0_1`
// and `…_1_1`, and only the attribute differs.  check.sh's shape arm pins
// both halves of that.
//
// Compared slice: the `theory … end` echo, which carries the `process=`
// attribute of every generated rule.  Every SAPIC condition in the corpus
// fits on one line, so no gate row reaches this shape.

theory SapicCondWrap
begin

functions: aaaaaaaaaa/1, bbbbbbbbbb/1, cccccccccc/1

predicates: Longer(xxxxxxxxxx, yyyyyyyyyy) <=> xxxxxxxxxx = yyyyyyyyyy

process:
  in(<xxxxxxxxxx, yyyyyyyyyy, zzzzzzzzzz>);
  if Longer(aaaaaaaaaa(xxxxxxxxxx), bbbbbbbbbb(yyyyyyyyyy)) & Longer(cccccccccc(zzzzzzzzzz), aaaaaaaaaa(yyyyyyyyyy)) then
     out('yes')
  else
     out('no')

end
